What I observed:
- Best anchors were tables under:
  - `Item 8. Financial Statements`
  - `Item 1. Financial Statements`
  - `Statements of Comprehensive Income`
  - `Statements of Income`
  - `Consolidated Statements of Income and Other Information`
- Good fallbacks:
  - `Selected Financial Data`
  - `Cash Flows` tables when they include a `Net income` row
- Important exclusions:
  - `Item 7` / MD&A
  - `Item 7A`
  - EPS notes
  - quarterly data notes

Notable document-specific patterns found:
- AMCOR answer came from `Net income attributable to Amcor plc` in MD&A/selected data, while a comprehensive income table had the wrong `437.4`.
- COSTCO 2017 ground truth aligned with `Net income available to common stockholders... 2,679`, not total net income `2,714`.
- FOOTLOCKER correct answer was in `Statements of Comprehensive Income` with `323`, while cash flow had `322`.
- COSTCO 2023 8-K had no relevant financial statements, so synthetic `None` is appropriate.

